-- title:
--   An exponential word bound for local graph counting
-- statement:
--   Let $h\in\mathbb N$ be the half-size parameter of the local subset graph. The declared integer-magnitude budget for the local counting procedure is
--   $W(h)=1024+4\bigl(2^{512h+1}\bigr)^2$. For every such $h$,
--
--   $$
--   W(h)\le 2^{1024h+11}.
--   $$
--
--   Here $W(h)$ is the bound on word values used by the machine contract, rather than a number of bits. The estimate applies also at $h=0$.
--
--   This places the concrete counting budget inside a simple exponential envelope that can be combined with the other local-parameter resource bounds.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LocalParameterBounds.lean#L103-L116

